\newlabel{fig:pascal}{{25.1}{359}{Left: each entry is the sum of the two above it, $\binom 42 = \binom 31 + \binom 32$. Right: the odd entries of the first 16 rows form a Sierpi\'nski triangle. By Lucas's theorem, $\binom {n}{k}$ is odd exactly when every 1-bit of $k$ is also a 1-bit of $n$: 81 of the 136 entries}{figure.caption.6}{}}
